MF=1  General Information                                         9543 1451   45
   -----------------------------------------------                9543 1451   46
                                                                  9543 1451   47
   The prompt fission neutron multiplicity and spectra            9543 1451   48
   are calculated using the BRC improved Los Alamos model from    9543 1451   49
   Vladuca and Tudora [2]. The model parameters are slightly      9543 1451   50
   different from those adopted in [2]. The prompt fission        9543 1451   51
   neutron multiplicity is obtained from an energetic balance     9543 1451   52
   ratio. The available energy (the average fission energy        9543 1451   53
   released minus the average fission fragment kinetic energy     9543 1451   54
   minus the average prompt gamma ray energy) is divided by the   9543 1451   55
   energy carry away by the neutron (the average fission          9543 1451   56
   fragment neutron separation energy plus the average            9543 1451   57
   center-of-mass energy of the emitted neutrons). The main       9543 1451   58
   improvement is the dependence of the average total             9543 1451   59
   fission-fragment kinetic energy and the average gamma energy   9543 1451   60
   on neutron incident energy.                                    9543 1451   61
                                                                  9543 1451   62
   MT=452 Total Nubar. Sum of MT=455 and 456                      9543 1451   63
   MT=455 23/11/2016  P. Leconte on behalf of CEA Reverted MF=1/5 9543 1451   64
          MT=455 to previous 8-group data from JEFF311            9543 1451   65
   MT=456 Prompt Neutron Yields.                                  9543 1451   66
   Vladuca and Tudora BRC improved Madland-Nix model              9543 1451   67
   MT=458 Energy Release. BRC modified ENDF/B-VII                 9543 1451   68
