MF=2  Resonance Parameters E < 150 eV                             9543 1451   71
   -----------------------------------------------                9543 1451   72
                                                                  9543 1451   73
   The resonance parameters were extracted from a simulatenous    9543 1451   74
   fit of the IRMM data (measurements started in 2007 in the      9543 1451   75
   frame of the PhD tesis of Christophe Sage) and of the EXFOR    9543 1451   76
   data (up to 150 eV).                                           9543 1451   77
                                                                  9543 1451   78
   The unresolved resonance parameters were calculated with the   9543 1451   79
   TALYS code (urr option) by using the average parameters        9543 1451   80
   deduced from the statistical analysis of the resonance         9543 1451   81
                                                                  9543 1451   82
                                                                  9543 1451   83
MF=3  Continuum Range E>40keV                                     9543 1451   84
   -----------------------------------------------                9543 1451   85
                                                                  9543 1451   86
   From the energy of 1 keV up to 200 MeV, eigth states :         9543 1451   87
     (ground-sate rotationnal band {5/2-,7/2-,9/2-,11/2-,13/2-}   9543 1451   88
      and octupolar band {5/2+,7/2+,9/2+})                        9543 1451   89
   Coupled Channel Calculations are performed using the ECIS06[3] 9543 1451   90
   code (implemented in the TALYS code [1])                       9543 1451   91
   which also provides compound nucleus cross sections and        9543 1451   92
   transmission coefficients used in pre-equilibrium/evaporation  9543 1451   93
   emission treated in the exciton and Hauser-Feshbach models     9543 1451   94
   implemented in the TALYS code [14]. This reaction includes also9543 1451   95
   width fluctuation factors,relativistic kinematic.Fission[4,5]  9543 1451   96
   penetrability model taking into account Triple Humped Fission  9543 1451   97
   Barrier (THFB) has been developed, explicitly coupling class   9543 1451   98
   I, II and III states while damping those of class II and III.  9543 1451   99
   Emission of light hadrons up to He4 are explicitly treated in  9543 1451  100
   the model calculations. Fission decay of associated residual   9543 1451  101
   nuclei is also treated.                                        9543 1451  102
