                                                                  9543 1451  218
For E<18KeV, the folowing methdology is applied:                  9543 1451  219
                                                                  9543 1451  220
   -------------------------------------------------------------- 9543 1451  221
   Capture Isomeric Ratio (IR) to 242Am ground and metastable     9543 1451  222
   states: new evaluation for JEFF3.2                             9543 1451  223
   -------------------------------------------------------------- 9543 1451  224
                         MF=10 MT=102                             9543 1451  225
                                                                  9543 1451  226
   Fluctuations of the IR are expected in the resolved resonance  9543 1451  227
   range (see [6,7]). This is called Spin Memory.                 9543 1451  228
                                                                  9543 1451  229
                                                                  9543 1451  230
   :::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::9543 1451  231
--> E < 100eV:                                                    9543 1451  232
                                                                  9543 1451  233
   Calculation results for s-waves [7] are the following:         9543 1451  234
                                                                  9543 1451  235
   IRmeta(Jpi=2-) = 0.0842+-0.0001                                9543 1451  236
   IRmeta(Jpi=3-) = 0.2271+-0.0002                                9543 1451  237
                                                                  9543 1451  238
   Below 100eV, we propose an energy-dependant isomeric ratio by a9543 1451  239
   straightforward linear combination of nuclear compound states  9543 1451  240
   described by a sum of single levels treated by the Breit-Wigner9543 1451  241
   formula. Thus, the amplitude coupling is not considered.       9543 1451  242
                                                                  9543 1451  243
   The spin assignement of the resonances are sampled             9543 1451  244
   by Monte Carlo technique and an optimum set of values is cho-  9543 1451  245
   -osen regarding to integral indirect measurements (Post-       9543 1451  246
   Irradiation Experiment analysis PIE) with following hypothesis:9543 1451  247
                                                                  9543 1451  248
   1- The gJxGn is maintained for each resonance.                 9543 1451  249
   2- A probability to reach each level is deduced.               9543 1451  250
   3- The mean isomeric ratio is obtained by convolution of IR(En)9543 1451  251
      and 241Am(n,gamma) calculated reaction rates                9543 1451  252
      (in the 281 SHEM multigroup format)                         9543 1451  253
   4- Integral Experiments are (Thermal point see above):         9543 1451  254
                                                                  9543 1451  255
       SHERWOOD (LWR like)           : <IRmeta> = 0.1090+-0.0020  9543 1451  256
       ICARE/S  (Undermoderated LWR) : <IRmeta> = 0.1640+-0.0040  9543 1451  257
                                                                  9543 1451  258
   PWR-PIE@High Burn-up are not considered here. Indeed,          9543 1451  259
   [242mAm]/[241Am] concentration ratio is sensititive to highly  9543 1451  260
   unknown 242mAm(n,absorption) thermal XS.                       9543 1451  261
                                                                  9543 1451  262
