MF=40  Variances of Isomeric Ratios (IR)                          9543 1451  313
   -----------------------------------------------                9543 1451  314
                                                                  9543 1451  315
   MT=102  Variances of the 241Am capture Isomeric Ratios (IR)    9543 1451  316
           to 242Am ground and metastable states [6]              9543 1451  317
                                                                  9543 1451  318
   The variances, here below, are tabulated only for the IR to    9543 1451  319
   the ground state since IR absolute variances for metastable    9543 1451  320
   and ground states are identical.                               9543 1451  321
                                                                  9543 1451  322
   The variances are essentially supplied by the 3 degrees error  9543 1451  323
   weighted polynomial fit which includes 3 components:           9543 1451  324
            - the estimated variance of the fitting;              9543 1451  325
   equal to the ratio of the residual sum of squares to the degree9543 1451  326
   of freedom,                                                    9543 1451  327
            - the variance resulting of the variances both on the 9543 1451  328
   fitting parameters and on the choice of our fitting law,       9543 1451  329
            - the Student's factor (statistical small sample      9543 1451  330
   theory by S.Gosset).                                           9543 1451  331
                                                                  9543 1451  332
   At very low energy where no experimental IR data or trends are 9543 1451  333
   available, the variance is arbitrarily set to the weighted     9543 1451  334
   average variance of the thermal data; Wisshak's point[9] at    9543 1451  335
   14.75meV included.                                             9543 1451  336
                                                                  9543 1451  337
   Above 300 keV where, again, no experimental IR data or trends  9543 1451  338
   are available, the variance of the polynomial fit is combined  9543 1451  339
   with the half difference between our fit normalized at 20 MeV  9543 1451  340
   to the IR to 242gAm value equal to 0.75 and another possible   9543 1451  341
   fit based on a normalization value of 0.5.                     9543 1451  342
                                                                  9543 1451  343
   Since the ENDF-6 rule do not allow pointwise variance data,    9543 1451  344
   the resulting pointwise variances were averaged over 11        9543 1451  345
   energy groups. The relative IR variances obtained [expressed   9543 1451  346
   in percent] are the following:                                 9543 1451  347
                                                                  9543 1451  348
   Energy groups     RelVar(IR to 242gAm)  RelVar(IR to 242mAm)   9543 1451  349
      [eV]               [percent]             [percent]          9543 1451  350
                                                                  9543 1451  351
   1.E-5 to 0.022          0.69                 7.05              9543 1451  352
